Records the #2300 remainder — a successful authorized non-loopback gateway call and distinct per-consumer caller identity — as verified live, in the OpenClaw comms design doc (G2 status in §2 and the follow-up status in §5). Doc-only change.\n\n## Evidence (2026-11-17, task 19760, from the laptop)\n\n- Probe client connected to the tailnet gateway (`ws://100.99.113.103:18789`) presenting the gateway token — fetched at probe time from the secrets-manager entry named `openclaw.gateway-token`, held only in the probe process's environment (no credential value in any file, doc, or chat) — completed the connect handshake (protocol v4; server 2026.10.7) and made an authorized `health` call: ok.\n- Two distinct named caller identities in the same run: `client.id` is the application class (`gateway-client`) in this build; per-consumer identity is `client.instanceId`. Authorized connect + `health` succeeded as instanceId `muse-gateway-client` and as instanceId `fleet-verification-probe`.\n- With the 2026-11-08 invalid-token rejection (close 1008, task 13141 / PR #7660), G2 is now verified in both directions on the tailnet bind.\n- Full evidence note: https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/2300#issuecomment-6943111371\n\nFixes #2300\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797496972&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=11164&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F11164&signature=4b41d3f7bae20d85a570341c4c388542deb1c2ec896ac816fe9c2cab574c63bb\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh